Subject: p-values calculated on beta values?
Message-ID: <eotpGTu8hgw.2C0TdKBUBwAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/eotpGTu8hgw/m/2C0TdKBUBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi, I'm trying to figure out if p-values are calculated (by logistic regression) on beta values directly when comparing two groups.  The confusion arises because calculateDiffMeth() uses the weighted values to determine delta beta, but it's not totally clear if the p-value for a given CpG are calculated based on the beta values from the individual samples belonging to the two groups.  Thank you, Rajat

